// EXPECT_STDOUT TARGET_MARKER 111
// EXPECT_STDOUT COLLIDE_RESULT 3
// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT OR Apache-2.0
// №TBD regression pin (бриф p617-name-scope, class "name resolves before
// scope", carrier №617).
//
// FACT (found by window p576 while drafting a #536 fixture, reported
// honestly out-of-scope): `import X as a` in one file makes `a` visible
// CU-WIDE (`TypeCheckCtx::build` collects `imported_modules`/
// `import_prefix_to_module_last` from EVERY peer file of the merged CU,
// `compiler-codegen/src/types/mod.rs` — the same reason #536's fix scopes
// `f1_check_call`'s `Member{obj: Ident(prefix)}` arm by `file_modules`) —
// unrelated local names `a`/`b` in a DIFFERENT file (e.g.
// `std/src/collections/vec/access.nv`'s `a.compare(b)`) share the same flat
// prefix set. NOT ESTABLISHED before this window: whether the leak causes
// a SILENT wrong-name pick, a LOUD collision, or nothing at all.
//
// OUTCOME, CHECKER (`types/mod.rs`, THIS window's zone) — CORRECT SCOPE:
// `f1_check_call`'s `Member{obj: Ident(prefix)}` arm checks
// `scope.contains_key(prefix)` FIRST — right before consulting
// `imported_modules` — so a local variable named the same as some OTHER
// file's import alias short-circuits there and resolves as an ordinary
// instance-method receiver; `imported_modules` is never even consulted.
// It has exactly ONE call site in the whole checker (this arm), always
// after the local-scope guard, so a local binding can never be shadowed by
// a same-named alias from another file. Verified directly: `nova check`
// PASSES on this fixture even when the alias below is renamed to
// `p617clash` — the EXACT spelling `p617_local_collide/mod.nv` uses for
// its own unrelated locals (checker output unaffected either way).
//
// OUTCOME, CODEGEN (`emit_c.rs` — OUT OF ZONE, read-only, NOT edited; see
// report first line) — GENUINE LOUD COLLISION, confirmed: renaming the
// alias below from `p617mod` to `p617clash` (so it EXACTLY matches
// `p617_local_collide/mod.nv`'s local `ro p617clash`) makes this fixture
// CC-FAIL: `p617_alias_leak_probe.c: error: use of undeclared identifier
// 'p617clash'`, generated as `nova_int t = p617clash.p617_target_marker;`
// — codegen misresolved the module-alias receiver as an instance-field
// access on the OTHER file's local variable. `nova check` still PASSES on
// that renamed variant (checker is right; only codegen goes wrong).
// Independently reproduced with NO second file at all: a bare
// `import p617_alias_target as a; fn main() { a.marker() }` also CC-FAILs
// (`a`/`b` specifically; `tgt`/`z`/`p617mod` do not) — std prelude
// (auto-imported into every CU) plausibly uses `a`/`b` as an ordinary
// local/param name somewhere, which is enough to poison the SAME
// mechanism. Root candidate: `CEmitter::var_types`
// (`compiler-codegen/src/codegen/emit_c.rs:798`, "Maps variable name -> C
// type string") is initialized ONCE (line 2584, `HashMap::new()`) and is
// NEVER `.clear()`-ed anywhere in the file (213 combined insert/remove
// call sites, no reset found) — a genuinely CU-WIDE, cross-FUNCTION,
// cross-FILE map. `infer_expr_c_type`'s `Ident` arm consults
// `var_types.get(name)` FIRST (line 62540) and only falls back to the
// correct `imported_modules.contains(name)` check LAST (line 62649) — a
// `var_types` entry left over from ANY earlier-compiled function using
// that bare name as a local (same file OR a completely different one)
// poisons every LATER use of that same spelling as a module alias. SAME
// class as #617 (name resolves before scope), a DIFFERENT table, in
// codegen rather than the checker — and LOUD (CC-FAIL leaking raw C), not
// silent.
//
// THIS fixture is kept GREEN and pinned to the checker-only claim (uses
// `p617mod`, a spelling that collides with nothing else in this CU) so it
// actually compiles, runs, and prints values (№577) instead of
// permanently CC-FAILing on a bug this window cannot fix (zone). The
// collision variant is described above precisely enough to reproduce
// (rename `p617mod` -> `p617clash` in the two `import`/call sites below)
// without committing a permanently-red fixture for a defect belonging to
// the parallel `emit_c.rs` window.

module standalone.p617_alias_leak_probe

import p617_alias_target as p617mod
import p617_local_collide

fn main() {
    ro t = p617mod.p617_target_marker()
    println("TARGET_MARKER ${t}")
    ro r = p617_local_collide.p617_run_collide()
    println("COLLIDE_RESULT ${r}")
}
